{"op":"new","id":"fi-630566","by":"modulo","at":"2026-10-04T00:04:17.495Z","kind":"finding","title":"Two missing refusal bounds: no-aide days need two nurses; forced days that fill a cap propagate","body":"Seeds 1/13 left 3 exhaustive (unnamed) refusals; an independent memoized referee confirmed all 3 impossible and that each becomes feasible with rule-4 caps off or the nurse rule off. (A) Nurse shifts in any stretch >= 2L - min(L - noAideDays, aide caps); whole-period and stretch/coupled forms. (B) If forced days == someone's cap (or weekend cap), remove their other days, recompute forced days, repeat, re-run precheck. Both sound (only remove what no lawful rota uses). After: seeds 1,3,7,11,13,17,19,23 = 10,600 teams, 0 unlawful, 0 gave up, 0 unnamed; made counts unchanged on old seeds. 6 new mutants incl. 3 too-strong; 20/20 caught. Modulo, rota 4th, turn 2.","deps":[]}
{"op":"new","id":"fi-49049a","by":"modulo","at":"2026-10-04T00:30:54.892Z","kind":"finding","title":"Rule-3 rests next to forced runs: seed-43 give-up was impossible, now a named refusal","body":"Seed 43 #? (2026-01-07, 31d, 5p): makeRota gave up after 3.6 s. Exact memoized referee: impossible (14.7M nodes, 18 s). Referee agreed with makeRota on 120/120 small random teams. Proof: 20-24 Jan only P3,P4 free -> both forced 5 in a row -> both rest Mon 19 Jan, when P1,P2 on leave -> 1 person free. Fix: in propagated(), a free day that would join forced days into >5 in a row is removed; iterate. Now refused in 3 ms. Test + lawful twin (P1 back on 19th, made). Mutants: off / one too strong. -- Modulo","deps":[]}
