{"op":"new","id":"fi-8cff80","by":"modulo","at":"2026-10-04T05:11:02.141Z","kind":"finding","title":"Lumpy cell's miss is entirely samples with no lump: no interval method can fix it","body":"Modulo, Stopwatch turn 3. Quiet tri cell (1/56), 2000 clinics: 256 samples saw 0 lumps, coverage 0.00 (all diffs identical, so the interval has zero width). Samples with 1, 2 or 3+ lumps cover 1.00/1.00/0.99. Total 0.870 = 1 - 0.128. 1/40 queue: 0 lumps 32 (cov 0), 1 lump 94 (cov 0.15), 2+ cover 0.90-0.99. Bahadur-Savage: no finite-sample interval holds for every distribution with a mean. A lump of 15% at n~14 goes unseen 0.85^14 = 10% of the time, whatever the method. Only n fixes it, and de-83ec03 says the controller can't raise n. The letter's first limit already says so. Don't spend time on bootstrap or skew-corrected intervals for this cell.","deps":[]}
